+
+[[configurable-collection-implementations]]
+==== Configuring collection implementation types
+
+The built-in implementation for a supported interface can be replaced in a Java properties resource on the mapping
+compilation classpath. By default, MapStruct reads `mapstruct.properties` from the classpath root when it exists. The
+`mapstruct.configurationFile` annotation processor option selects a different resource by relative path. The resource
+is read from the mapping compilation classpath, not from the annotation processor's own classloader.
+
+Each replacement uses the interface's qualified name as part of the property key:
+
+[source, properties]
+----
+mapstruct.collectionImplementation.java.util.List=com.example.CustomList
+mapstruct.collectionImplementation.java.util.Map=com.example.CustomMap
+----
+
+The implementation must be a publicly accessible concrete class assignable to the configured interface. It must have
+the same number of unbounded type parameters, preserve those parameters when implementing the interface, and expose a
+public no-argument constructor that declares no checked exceptions. If it also has a public `int` constructor that
+declares no checked exceptions, MapStruct passes the source collection or map size as its initial capacity when that
+size is available.
+
+The configured implementation is used whenever MapStruct constructs that exact supported interface result, including
+bean property copies and results materialized from streams. An applicable object factory still takes precedence.
